// EV1 (note 46): part 4 of 4, Sunday Day 63, the end. Chapters twenty to the end: the storm of the century; the
// lamp's motor dies; Ada and Quill turn the lens by hand all night and a ship finds the harbour. At dawn Quill gives
// her the log and goes with the boatman. Ada writes the first entry: "To whoever comes after". Esme says the next
// showing is everyone's own books again. Your answer flags read.s4.<k> (nothing reads it yet).
title: Reading corner: The Lighthouse at Coriel
from: Esme Walsh
gist: Reading corner finished The Lighthouse at Coriel together.
== lines
walsh-esme: The end. Everyone finished? Everyone?
ibarra-rafael: Finished. First book I've finished all tour.
soto-marta: The motor dies in the storm. Course it does.
soto-marta: Turning the lens by hand, all night. Proper work.
strand-erik: And the ship sees the light, and finds the harbour.
kowalczyk: I read that bit first. Years ago. Still got me.   [sigh]
strand-erik: Then he just hands her the log and gets in the boat.
ibarra-rafael: I may have cried. Briefly. On shift.
soto-marta: Fine. It was good. Don't tell anyone I said so.
walsh-esme: Her first entry. "To whoever comes after."
kowalczyk: Every ship's a bit like that light. Someone's always on.
walsh-esme > you: What did you think of the ending?
? choice
* It's the right ending.   rel:walsh-esme+1 flag:read.s4.1
